{"header":"<h1>Module <code><span>Objective.Value</span></code></h1>","type":"documentation","uses_katex":false,"breadcrumbs":[{"name":"Index","href":"../../../../index.html","kind":"leaf-page"},{"name":"alt-ergo-lib","href":"../../../index.html","kind":"page"},{"name":"AltErgoLib","href":"../../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Objective","href":"../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Value","href":"#","kind":"module"}],"toc":[],"source_anchor":null,"preamble":"","content":"<div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec type anchored\" id=\"type-limit_kind\"><a href=\"#type-limit_kind\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">type</span> limit_kind</span><span> = </span></code><ol><li id=\"type-limit_kind.Above\" class=\"def variant constructor anchored\"><a href=\"#type-limit_kind.Above\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span>| </span><span><span class=\"constructor\">Above</span></span></code></li><li id=\"type-limit_kind.Below\" class=\"def variant constructor anchored\"><a href=\"#type-limit_kind.Below\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span>| </span><span><span class=\"constructor\">Below</span></span></code><div class=\"def-doc\"><span class=\"comment-delim\">(*</span><p>Type used to discriminate between limits from above or below.</p><span class=\"comment-delim\">*)</span></div></li></ol></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec type anchored\" id=\"type-t\"><a href=\"#type-t\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">type</span> t</span><span> = </span></code><ol><li id=\"type-t.Minfinity\" class=\"def variant constructor anchored\"><a href=\"#type-t.Minfinity\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span>| </span><span><span class=\"constructor\">Minfinity</span></span></code></li><li id=\"type-t.Pinfinity\" class=\"def variant constructor anchored\"><a href=\"#type-t.Pinfinity\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span>| </span><span><span class=\"constructor\">Pinfinity</span></span></code></li><li id=\"type-t.Value\" class=\"def variant constructor anchored\"><a href=\"#type-t.Value\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span>| </span><span><span class=\"constructor\">Value</span> <span class=\"keyword\">of</span> <a href=\"../../Expr/index.html#type-t\">Expr.t</a></span></code></li><li id=\"type-t.Limit\" class=\"def variant constructor anchored\"><a href=\"#type-t.Limit\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span>| </span><span><span class=\"constructor\">Limit</span> <span class=\"keyword\">of</span> <a href=\"#type-limit_kind\">limit_kind</a> * <a href=\"../../Expr/index.html#type-t\">Expr.t</a></span></code><div class=\"def-doc\"><span class=\"comment-delim\">(*</span><p>This case occurs when we try to optimize a strict bound. For instance, we have a constraint of the form <code>x &lt; 2</code>, there is no maximum for <code>x</code> but <code>2</code> is an upper bound. So <code>2</code> is a limit from below of the possible model values.</p><span class=\"comment-delim\">*)</span></div></li><li id=\"type-t.Unknown\" class=\"def variant constructor anchored\"><a href=\"#type-t.Unknown\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span>| </span><span><span class=\"constructor\">Unknown</span></span></code><div class=\"def-doc\"><span class=\"comment-delim\">(*</span><p>The value of the objective function has not yet been determined.</p><span class=\"comment-delim\">*)</span></div></li></ol></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-pp\"><a href=\"#val-pp\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> pp : <span><a href=\"#type-t\">t</a> <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Fmt</span>.t</span></span></code></div></div>"}